# Site configuration for the submit-*.sh launchers. Copy to `local.env`, which is
# untracked; each launcher sources it if present:
#
#   cp dataset/local.env.example dataset/local.env
#
# Each entry keeps a value already in the environment, so a one-off
# `PART=... ./submit-verify.sh` still wins.

# Slurm partition for the dataset jobs; empty means the site's default.
PART="${PART:-}"

# Nodes to keep the dataset jobs off, comma-separated. A benchmark node whose
# page cache is a recorded measurement constant belongs here: streaming hundreds
# of GB of raw text through it would silently corrupt a timing.
EXCLUDE="${EXCLUDE:-}"
